  Title: 40+ radiologists leaving a CT hospital in less than two months. ‘Should be on the radar’: lawmaker
  Source: courant.com
  URL: https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxNdkt2N0tvcnFub1llY05PVEFwdHBJR1g4Uy1hQTZjaDFfSFROUVlmUmRZd1hBdkxxNWdGbmp2M09kSVE3b0xRZHFqNFp5dXJ4TEVYdmNQRlN5RzJLWGliVVd3bUNaa3R5YnFmdmFCdExoNnZ6X0Q5NVNTTmdqZVczM1A3TXV1ZXFDNmtUbXZ1blRkVlBheDRNZlluTWI4UUFicFExRVhyMGJHeGM?oc=5
  category: news
  importance: 95
  ai_summary: "A significant exodus of radiologists from a CT hospital in a short period raises concerns about workforce stability and potential impacts on patient care. This trend highlights a critical issue in radiology staffing across the country."
  
  Title: Scientists may have been wrong about what causes asthma
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260127010147.htm
  category: research
  importance: 90
  ai_summary: "New research suggests asthma might not be driven by the previously blamed molecules but by 'pseudo leukotrienes,' offering a potential shift in understanding and treatment approaches. This could lead to novel therapies that target the inflammatory spark rather than just the aftermath."
  
  Title: Scientists found a survival switch inside brain cells
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260127010138.htm
  category: research
  importance: 85
  ai_summary: "Researchers have identified a mechanism where sugar metabolism can either promote neuronal collapse or survival, hinting at new therapeutic avenues for neurodegenerative diseases. This finding could allow for interventions to protect vulnerable brain cells."
  
  Title: Obesity and high blood pressure may directly cause dementia
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260126231847.htm
  category: research
  importance: 80
  ai_summary: "A genetic study indicates a direct link between obesity, high blood pressure, and dementia, suggesting these conditions damage the brain over time. This challenges the previous understanding of risk and opens doors for preventative strategies."
  
  Title: Keto diet weight loss may come with a hidden cost
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260127010144.htm
  category: research
  importance: 75
  ai_summary: "A long-term study reveals that while a keto diet can aid in weight loss, it can also trigger metabolic problems like fatty liver disease and impaired blood sugar control. This suggests potential long-term risks associated with this dietary approach."
  
